window.WIKI_ENTRY={"id": "concept-006", "name_zh": "自我", "name_en": "ego", "tagline": "在赛斯体系里，你每天以为的「我」（自我）其实只是「自己」的一小片——它负责在物质世界里帮你组织经验，却不是你的全部身份；把它当成全部，就容易把自己困住。", "explanation": "在赛斯体系里，「自我（ego）」是你每天认同的那个「我」，但它只是「自己（self）」的一小片，不是你的全部身份，也不是意识本身。赛斯把自我分成两层：向内运作、形成个体并握有心理蓝图的内我，和向外在物质世界里组织经验、像看门狗一样留守的外我——前者是后者的源头，外我只是内我的影子。自我的本职是聚焦与组织：它把涌进意识心的材料排序、对物理实相做实质操纵、维持物质世界的稳定外观，却无法把信息挡在意识之外，只能选择不把注意力放上去。它最大的陷阱是把目标和才能据为己有、误以为自己就是全部，于是把失败怪给命运、把自己关在狭隘的实相里；但一个通情达理、有纪律、懂得放松的自我，反而是「一切万有」高度专门化、让你得以解读物质状况的那一片。人类投射出去的「神」，本质上也是正在浮现的自我之反映。自我死后不会消失，只是形态改变——新的自我从旧自我的死亡里诞生，像小孩一样慢慢长成。", "definitions": [{"zh": "许多人想象灵魂就是一个不朽化了的自我，却忘了你所知的自我只是自己的一小部分；也就是说，人格的这一段就这么永无止境地被继续投射下去。由于你们很少了解到你们实相的幅度，所以你们的观念必然是很狭窄的。在想到“不朽”时，人类似乎希望发展出更长远的自我，但他又反对这种发展可能涉及改变的观念。经由他的宗教，他说他的确是有灵魂的，却问都没问灵魂是什么，再次的，他似乎常常把它当作是他拥有的一样物件。", "en": "Many individuals imagine the soul to be an immortalized ego, forgetting that the ego as you know it is only a small portion of the self; so this section of the personality is simply projected onward, ad infinitum, so to speak. Because the dimensions of your reality are so little understood, your concepts are bound to be limited. In considering “immortality,” mankind seems to hope for further egotistical development, and yet he objects to the idea that such development might involve change. He says through his religions that he has a soul indeed, without even asking what a soul is, and often he seems to regard it, again, as an object in his possession.", "source": "Session 527"}, {"zh": "显然，自我是本体的一部分，而不是相反，它只是意识的一部分。当自我试图把自己与本体混为一谈时，困难就开始了。", "en": "Obviously then ego is a part of identity, rather than the other way around, and it is only a part of consciousness. It is when ego attempts to confuse itself with identity that difficulties begin.", "source": "Session 460"}, {"zh": "自我专长于空间的扩展及空间上的实质操纵。它专长于物体。", "en": "The ego specialized in expansions of space and its physical manipulation. It specialized with objects.", "source": "Session 686"}], "blocks": [{"id": "B01", "title": "「自我」到底是谁？它只是「自己」的一小片", "note": "赛斯反复提醒：你习惯认同的那个「我」，只是「自己（self）」的一小部分，不是你的全部本体。早期课里他就说潜意识与自我其实是一体，自我是潜意识为了达成目标而投射出来的工具；到《灵魂永生》他更直接点破，很多人把灵魂想成「不朽化了的自我」，却忘了所知的自我只是自己的一小段。所以身份（本体）并不主要住在自我里——社会身份或许在，但基本身份不在。你也别把自我和意识划等号：它是意识的一部分，不是意识本身。你比你所认同的那个日常之我大得多，那些不被你的自我觉察到的部分，活在一个更强的能量层次里，你过去的所有生命都活在你里面。", "src": "第 17、227、240、255、273、311、460、511、527、530、558、575 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 17 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 227 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 240 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 255 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 273 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 311 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 460 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 511 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 527 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 530 节"}, {"n": 11, "id": null, "label": "第 558 节"}, {"n": 12, "id": null, "label": "第 575 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-006-e0025", "zh": "你看，亲爱的约瑟，潜意识和自我，两者当然都是你。为了简便起见，我才会说自我和潜意识，它们实际上是一体。潜意识形成并投射自我这个工具的物质化，好让它达成目标。如果把这些目标和才能单独地归属于自我，那可以说等于把它们砍了头。", "en": "You see, dear Joseph, the subconscious and the ego, of course, are both you. For simplicity’s sake I will speak of the ego and the subconscious, though they are actually one. The subconscious forms and projects the materializations of the ego as a tool to enable it to attain its goals. When these goals and talents are attributed to the ego alone they are so to speak decapitated.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第17节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "17", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e0856", "zh": "你们所知道的自我，你们时间系统里有意识的自己，比如说，这个自我达到且经验了事件X。", "en": "The ego as you know it, the conscious self within your time system, this ego, let us say, arrives at and experiences event X.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第227节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "227", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e0915", "zh": "在物质存在期间，自己并不是你想像的那样永久依附着肉体。 自我比人格的其他部分更依赖肉身自己。肉体更像是总站，由此出发从事频繁的短途旅行。自我就像留在家中的守护者。有如看门狗。", "en": "The self does not remain as permanently attached to the physical body as you imagine, during physical existence. The ego is much more dependent upon the physical self than are other portions of the personality. The physical body is more like a home station, from which frequent excursions are made. The ego is like a guardian who is left at home, as watchdog.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第240节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "240", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e0946", "zh": "我们要把这两个主题结合在一起。这本书应该说明一点：尽管表面看来全部相反，但是本体主要并不是存在自我中。社会本体可能存在那里，但基本本体不是。", "en": "We shall tie these two subjects together. The book should make one point plain: Identity, despite all appearances to the contrary, does not reside primarily in the ego. Social identity may possibly there reside, but the basic identity does not.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第255节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "255", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1008", "zh": "你不认识在物质存在之内的自己，在你认识它之前，你无从得知在肉体死亡之后存活下来的是什么，或在自我睡着时，醒着的是你的哪一部分。当我提到自我时，我是为了简单起见才这么说，因为这个字眼对你有意义。显然，自己的某些部分永远不会在物质实相中直接运作。", "en": "You do not know the self as it is within physical existence, and until you do you cannot hope to know what survives physical death, or what part of you is awake while the ego sleeps. When I refer to the ego I do so for simplicity’s sake, since the term has meaning to you. There are obviously portions of the self that never operate directly within physical reality.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第273节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "273", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1101", "zh": "你对这个事实的了悟程度就是你的自由或生命力、（价值）完成与力量的幅度。然而，不应该忘记的是，自我也是一切万有的一部分，一个高度专门化的部分，它让内我得以操纵和解读特定的状况。如果自我认为它自己是唯一的自己，那你就会有很大的程度无法汲取可得的生命力和能量。", "en": "The extent of your realization of this fact is the extent of your freedom or vitality, fulfillment and power. It should not be forgotten, however, that the ego is also a portion of All That Is, a highly specialized portion, enabling the inner self to manipulate and interpret particular conditions. If the ego considers itself as the only self, then you are cut off to a large degree from the vitality and energy available.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第311节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "311", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1297", "zh": "那么显然，自我是本体的一部分，而不是相反，它只是意识的一部分。当自我试图把自己与本体混为一谈时，困难就开始了。", "en": "Obviously then ego is a part of identity, rather than the other way around, and it is only a part of consciousness. It is when ego attempts to confuse itself with identity that difficulties begin.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第460节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "460", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1381", "zh": "许多人想象灵魂就是一个不朽化了的自我，却忘了你所知的自我只是自己的一小部分；也就是说，人格的这一段就这么永无止境地被继续投射下去。由于你们很少了解到你们实相的幅度，所以你们的观念必然是很狭窄的。在想到“不朽”时，人类似乎希望发展出更长远的自我，但他又反对这种发展可能涉及改变的观念。经由他的宗教，他说他的确是有灵魂的，却问都没问灵魂是什么，再次的，他似乎常常把它当作是他拥有的一样物件。", "en": "Many individuals imagine the soul to be an immortalized ego, forgetting that the ego as you know it is only a small portion of the self; so this section of the personality is simply projected onward, ad infinitum, so to speak. Because the dimensions of your reality are so little understood, your concepts are bound to be limited. In considering “immortality,” mankind seems to hope for further egotistical development, and yet he objects to the idea that such development might involve change. He says through his religions that he has a soul indeed, without even asking what a soul is, and often he seems to regard it, again, as an object in his possession.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第527节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "527", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1417", "zh": "不过，当你让你的注意力动摇的时候，你可能常常落入一种状态，在其中你暂时对另一个替代的现在看到几眼。全我——灵魂——知道它在所有这些系统中的实相；而你，作为其一部分，正向着同样的自我觉察与发展的状态努力。", "en": "When you let your attention waver, however, you may often fall into a state in which you momentarily perceive glimpses of another alternate present. The whole self, the soul, knows of its reality in all such systems, and you, as a part of it, are working toward the same state of self-awareness and development.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第575节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "575", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1441", "zh": "你们都曾在他种生存的层面中活过，你们内心明白，但是也许目前的“自我”却意识不到。我希望这本书能唤醒每一位读者的内心，给你们最适当的启示。", "en": "You have each lived other existences, and that knowledge is within you though you are not consciously aware of it. I hope that this book will serve to release the deeply intuitive self within each of my readers, and to bring to the foreground of consciousness whatever particular insights will serve you most.", "source": "时空之外 · 第511节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "时空之外", "session": "511", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1469", "zh": "所以其他部分的你——也就是不为你的自我意识所知的你——住在一个可以称之为“超级系统”的世界中，而你正在那里学习处理及认知更强的浓缩能量，同时学习去架构不同性质的“形相”。", "en": "Other portions of yourself, therefore, of which you are not consciously aware, do inhabit what you could call a supersystem of reality in which consciousness learns to handle and perceive much stronger concentrations of energy, and to construct “forms” of a different nature indeed.", "source": "时空之外 · 第530节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "时空之外", "session": "530", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1498", "zh": "所有你自己的“过去”现在都在你自己里面，因而你就能把自己的回忆抓回来，而找出这些“过去”究竟都是些什么东西。你绝不会为“时间”所困，除非你相信“时间”能困得往你，没有什么比“信”更重要的事情。如果你相信自己只有这一辈子，认为这辈子就是从“生”到“死”、到“绝灭”，别无其他的话，那么你就白白放过了你这一生中所拥有的自由。即使是当这些自在的自我显现出来的时候，你还是会因为自己“信”之所限而否定了自己这些自由的能力。并没有谁强加这些枷锁在你身上，这么做的只有你自己。如果你想对自己那多重空间层次的“大我”有所认识，你就必须先去用它。", "en": "Now: All of your so-called pasts exist within you now, and you can recapture your memories and discover what they are. You are not imprisoned in time unless you believe that you are, and there is nothing more important than belief. If you believe that you exist only within the context of this life, that you are born only to death and annihilation, then you will not use your freedoms in this existence. You deny their abilities when they show themselves, yet no one forces this bondage upon you but yourself. To understand your multidimensional self is to use it.", "source": "时空之外 · 第558节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "时空之外", "session": "558", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B02", "title": "外我与内我：其实是两层「自我」", "note": "赛斯把自我分成两层来讲：向内运作的「内在自我（内我）」和向外面对物质世界的「外在自我（外我）」。内我是你的对等物，它把能量拆解成分子原子、形成个体，并持续运转、永远在「成为」的状态里，包含着你这一世全部潜力的心理蓝图；外我则负责在物质环境里摆布自己，是那个留在家里看门的守护者。两者不是上下级，而是相互依存的完形：主导的自我会影响内在本体，内在本体也影响和改变主导的自我。前台你以为的「我」，本质上是内我的一个影子，而不是反过来。在梦与投射里活跃的是内我，外我几乎不参与；内我还不受理性与因果的限制，在更广的框架里推理与安排事件。", "src": "第 50、55、58、119、162、177、242、256、270、509、822、823、894 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 50 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 55 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 58 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 119 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 162 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 177 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 242 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 256 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 270 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 509 节"}, {"n": 11, "id": null, "label": "第 822 节"}, {"n": 12, "id": null, "label": "第 823 节"}, {"n": 13, "id": null, "label": "第 894 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-006-e0202", "zh": "所以内在自我是你们的对等物（counterpart）。它把能量拆解成简单的成分，但它仍然得在内在宇宙既有的法则之内运作。于是它形成将构成个体的个别分子和原子。它本身的知识被放进浓缩的形式之中，分子因此能够依据你们宇宙固有的物质特性结合与再结合。", "en": "The inner ego therefore is your counterpart. It breaks energy down into simple components, but it must still operate within the given laws of the inner universe. It therefore forms the separate molecules and atoms that will compose the individual. Its own knowledge is put into condensed form, and the molecules are therefore able to combine and recombine, according to the material properties inherent in your universe.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第50节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "50", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e0218", "zh": "自己会真的利用原子和分子；意识会以这种方式旅行。然后这个肉体于是会以它所是被人认识：一个共同合作的心灵完形，一个内在自我利用本身就活生生、有意识的原子和分子，一起形成的心灵-物质结构。", "en": "The self will truly utilize the atoms and molecules; the consciousness will travel by this method. The particular physical body will then be known for what it is: a cooperative psychic gestalt, a psychio-physical structure formed together by the inner ego, utilizing atoms and molecules that are in themselves living and conscious.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第55节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "55", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e0235", "zh": "我可以想像，这非常难以理解。但是，即使当一个内我送出了一个新的外在自我去进行一个新的伪装冒险，先前的自我还是有几近无限的发展途径。它有很多可能性。它可以选择保持现况，一个自我。然后留在一个有点附属于内我的位置上，但一点都不比它以前的附属地位低。", "en": "This is extremely difficult, I should imagine. Nevertheless, even when an inner self has sent out a new outer ego upon a new camouflage venture, the previous ego is still afforded an almost unlimited avenue for development. There are many possibilities for it. It can choose to remain what it is, one ego. It will then remain in a somewhat subordinate position to the inner self, but in no more of a subordinate position than it was earlier.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第58节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "58", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e0376", "zh": "在很多方面，它是一个反映者，自己那往外看的表面。虽然这是必要的，但自己整个剩下来的部分不能留给一个没有把注意力集中在深处之内，而是坐在房子的前廊，丢着内在工作不管的组织者或照顾者。外在自我不想要见到内在自我。外在自我不想要承认内在自我的存在。就像没有镜子，眼睛看不到它自己的瞳孔，同样的，要不是内在自我藏在所有倒影的深处，外在自我连它自己都看不到。", "en": "In many respects it is a reflector, the surface of the self looking outward. While this is necessary, the whole remainder of the self could not be left to an organizer or caretaker who did not focus his attentions within the depths but sat, as it were, on the front porch of the house, leaving the inner workings unattended. The outer ego does not want to meet the inner ego. The outer ego does not want to admit the existence of the inner ego. As the eye cannot see its own pupil without a mirror, so the outer ego could not even see itself, were it not that the inner ego hides in the depths of all reflections.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第119节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "119", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e0619", "zh": "我不想在一时之间跟你们讲太多细节。不过，我们或许可以把内在自我看成是另一张向内看的脸，我们正在打个比喻，这个比喻的目的纯粹是为了简化。因此我们可以说，从外在环境来看，你们先有你们认为是自我的这一部分，而这部分我会称它为外在自我。", "en": "Then, according to our analogy, you will find the subconscious areas; and these areas may be, briefly, differentiated in the following manner.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第162节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "162", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e0699", "zh": "内在自我会指引所有高度主观的活动。而外在自我，如你们所知，会在物质环境中负责自己。你们必须记得，全我大于各部分的总合；而且，由于全我就是行动，所以它时时刻刻都不一样。因此不管什么时候，要精确定位人格是不可能的。全我不只是你们在你们时间内所认识的人格之总和，也是它曾经所是与未来所是的总和。因为就如我之前的解释，行动具有同时性，而时间正如你们所以为的，是由你们自己的身体知觉所形成。", "en": "The inner ego directs all activities which are deeply subjective. The outer ego as you know deals with the manipulation of the self in the physical environment. You must remember that the whole self is more than the sum of its parts; and also, since it is action, it is never the same. It is therefore impossible at any moment to pinpoint the personality. Therefore the whole self is not only the sum of the personality as you know it in your time, it is also the sum of what it has been and what it shall be. For as I have explained action is simultaneous, and time as you think of it is caused by your own physical perception.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第177节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "177", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e0930", "zh": "在我与你的通讯中，我是以全我的身分讲话，而不是在其他存在中居于主导地位的任何一个自我。如果我在你们现在这一世的物质时间之内认识同时代的你们其中一人，那么在死后我会再一次采用你们已经认识的这个主导自我。然而，我并没有被任何强烈的情感连结束缚在物质存在上，而且我的人格结构也比其他系统的传播者更为先进。", "en": "In my communications to you, I speak as my whole self, and not on the part of any one of the egos which have been dominant in other existences. If I had known either of you as contemporaries within your physical time in your present existence, then after death I would have assumed, once again, the dominant ego by which you had known me. I am not tied to physical existence by any strong emotional bonds however, and my personality structure is more advanced than is usual for communicators from other systems.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第242节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "242", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e0961", "zh": "即使内在本体会影响和改变主导的自我，但是自我，占主导地位的自我的确会影响也会改变内在本体。因为我们这里毕竟是在处理一个相互依存的完形。整个完形的交互作用从未被完全了解过。", "en": "Now, the ego, the dominant ego, does indeed affect the inner identity, and changes it even as it affects and changes the dominant ego. For we are dealing here after all with an interdependent gestalt. The interworking’s of the whole gestalt have never been completely understood.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第256节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "256", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e0992", "zh": "在这样的梦中，你的感知似乎清晰至极，你可以确定内在自我正在运作。现在，人格，现有人格的所有部分，都属于这个内在自我。它持续不断运转，但始终处于变为的状态。它不只是你在你们的时间当中任何既定时刻的你所是而已。它包含而且就是心理蓝图，现有人格在任何既定的转世之内的全部潜力就包含在这个蓝图之中。", "en": "When in such dreams your perceptions seem exceedingly clear, you can be certain that the inner ego is operating. Now all portions of the personality, of the present personality, belong to this inner ego. It functions constantly, and yet it is always in a state of becoming. It is more than what you are at any given moment in your time. It contains, and j^, the psychological blueprint containing the full potential of the present personality within any given incarnation.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第270节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "270", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1342", "zh": "再说，内我所做的一切丰饶的创造性工作、一切原创的工作，都不是无意识的。那是有目的的、高度明辨的，由内在的有意识自我执行的——外在的自我只是它的一个影子，你们明白，而不是倒过来。", "en": "Now all the richly creative, original work that is done by this inner self is not unconscious. It is purposeful, highly (underlined) discriminating, performed by the inner conscious ego, of which the exterior ego is but a shadow, and not you see the other way around.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第509节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "509", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1759", "zh": "它就是那个向外看的自己，它就是你称为自我性的觉察的自己。内我变成了我所谓的内在自我。它看入你自己的意识及你身体的意识两者由之浮露的那个内在实相，那觉性的心灵次元。", "en": "It is the self that looks outward. It is the self that you call egotistically aware. The inner self became what I refer to as the inner ego. It looks into that inner reality, that psychic dimension of awareness from which both your own consciousness and your body consciousness emerged.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第894节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "894", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1738", "zh": "如果你想改变工作，而心怀那个欲望，一个新的工作就会以完全同样的方式进入你的经验，因为内在事件会由内我来安排。一件身体上的事件涉及了许多肌肉关节等等的作用。就如涉及工作改变的一个事件也关系到许多人的动作，并且暗示了所有牵涉到的内我的一个沟通网。那么，显然的，一个具体的群体事件暗示了一种在比例上会把你们科技性沟通比下去的内在沟通系统。", "en": "If you want to change your job, and hold that desire, a new job will come into your experience in precisely the same fashion, in that the inner events will be arranged by the inner ego. A body event involves the working of numerous muscles and joints and so forth. An event involving a job change concerns motion on the part of many people, and implies a network of communication on the part of all of the inner egos involved. Obviously, then, a mass physical event implies an inner system of communications of proportions that would put your technological communications to shame.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第822节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "822", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1743", "zh": "我说内我会推理，但其推理并不受限于因与果之限制。内我在“架构二”的较广范围内之行动，解释了许多在你们世界里本来仿佛不合理的事件及看起来的巧合。在“架构二”之内的许多实相，无法适当的在“架构一”里向你解释为事实，只因为它们涉及了无法被转译为如你所认为的事实之心理厚度。反之，这些常常以艺术的象征语言出现，而你们许多的梦都是一种转译，在其中，“架构二”的事件以象征形式出现。", "en": "I said that the inner ego reasons, but its reasoning is not restricted to the cause-and-effect limitations that you apply to the reasoning process. The action of the inner ego within the wider sphere of Framework 2 explains many events and seeming coincidences that otherwise seem to make no sense within your world. Many realities within Framework 2 cannot suitably be explained as facts to you in Framework 1, simply because they involve psychological thicknesses that cannot be translated into facts as you think of them. These often appear in the symbolic language of the arts instead, and many of your dreams are translations in which the events of Framework 2 appear in symbolic form.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第823节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "823", "only_en": true}]}]}, {"id": "B03", "title": "自我是干嘛用的：组织与聚焦物质实相的工具", "note": "自我的本职是「组织与聚焦」。它把涌进意识心的材料整理排序，对物理实相做特定的集中与实质操纵——它专长于物体、空间，所以你才能在同一时刻知道地球另一端发生了什么，尽管身体已无法像面对猛兽那样即刻反应。它是伪装实相里的积木：永远不会少于一个单位，也可能变成更多。但它无法把信息挡在意识心之外，只能选择不把注意力直接聚焦上去。意识最初创造了物质维度，而你的身体形象与环境，都是内在自我延伸出来的具体化物——自我只是这台合作工程里负责物质这一头的那部分，它看似独立于行动，其实自己就是行动。", "src": "第 31、59、86、139、338、343、409、616、686 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 31 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 59 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 86 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 139 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 338 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 343 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 409 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 616 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 686 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-006-e0097", "zh": "然后，为了建构伪装实相，意识自我会操纵这些材料。面向内在世界的自我意识自己，会将生命力转化为物质道具。潜意识连结了这两种自我意识，而这时候你们也即将发现伪装人格接受了这些材料。", "en": "The conscious ego then manipulates this material for the purposes of camouflage constructions. The transformation of vitality into physical properties is done by this self-conscious self that faces the inner world. The subconscious is the link between these two self-consciousness, and here you find an acceptance by the camouflage personality of the materials at hand.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第31节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "31", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e0251", "zh": "你们已经看到自我是一块积木。它从来不会少于一个单位，并且可能变成更多。", "en": "You have seen that the ego is a building block. It never becomes less than a unit, and may become more.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第59节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "59", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e0285", "zh": "这个系统或精神围场，再说一次，只是相对来说是封闭的。关闭一个层面的一个通道，并让替代或内在通讯管道保持开放，这要花一番工夫。这里打个比方，意识自我可以说是存在这个铜管之内，差不多位于它的正中央。", "en": "The system or the mental enclosure, again, is only closed comparatively speaking. An endeavor is made to close one opening from one plane, and keep the alternate or inner communication channel open. As an analogy here, the conscious ego could be said to exist within this copper tube, located at approximately its center.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第86节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "86", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e0437", "zh": "但自我看似不依赖行动的独立，基本上毫无意义。因为自我也是行动，而且绝不可能不是。它自己与行动的任何这类分离，只会增加行动的总额，因为它提高了行动从尽可能多的观点感知它自己的能力。视角（perspectives）代表行动对它自己采取的行动。任何一个维度都一定会产生另一个维度，因为在任何既定维度之内的行动，绝不可能完成它自己，而是会继续下去。", "en": "But ego’s seeming independence from action is basically meaningless, since ego is also action, and can never be otherwise. Any such separation of action from itself only adds to the totality of action, in that it increases actions ability to perceive itself from as many viewpoints as possible. Perspectives represent action’s action upon itself. Any one dimension must result in another dimension, for the action within any given dimension can never complete itself, but will continue.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第139节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "139", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1225", "zh": "我们就以你们的物质系统为例。在这个系统里面，有着整体所有自我结构都会关注的焦点，由于这个焦点具有足够的约束力与凝聚力，因此外观上可以保持永久且普遍存在的物质实相。结构中的自我部分，在那些形成物质实相的坐标内，会聚精会神做自我引导。", "en": "We will take your physical system as an example. There is general and mass focus of all self structures within that system, binding enough and cohesive enough so that the appearance of a permanent and all-pervading physical reality is maintained. The ego part of the structure concentrates with great intensity, directing itself within those coordinates that form physical reality.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第409节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "409", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1570", "zh": "自我试着把所有进入意识心的资料加以组织整理，因为自我的目的就是处理任何时候，当“我”接触物质实相后，浮现到表面来的东西。如我曾说的，自我无法切断来自意识心的资料，但是它可以拒绝直接聚焦于其上。", "en": "The ego tries to organize all material coming into the conscious mind, for its purposes — the ego’s — are those that have come to the surface at any given time in the self’s overall encounter with physical reality. As I said, the ego cannot keep information out of the conscious mind but it can refuse to focus directly upon it.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第616节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "616", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1654", "zh": "自我专长于空间的扩展及空间上的实质操纵。它专长于物体。于是，其结果是一个在任何既定时间里的人对世界另一端所发生的事件是觉察的。他能做的即刻身体反应在许多场合看起来都不适宜或不切题了。那么，到那个程度，身体的具体行动在时间里失掉了它纯净的精确性。你无法踢一个不住在你村里或国家里的“敌人”；尤其是一个你个人甚至不认识的敌人。（热切的：）再次的，到那个程度，在时间里即刻的身体行动已不再具有当一个人在与一个被激怒的动物、或敌人短兵相接时同样生死交关的因素。", "en": "The ego specialized in expansions of space and its physical manipulation. It specialized with objects. As a result, now, a person in any given hour is aware of events happening at the other end of the world. No immediate physical response he or she can make seems adequate or pertinent on many occasions. Bodily physical action, then, to that extent, loses its immaculate precision in time. You cannot kick an “enemy” who does not live in your village or country; an enemy, furthermore, whom you do not even know personally. (Intently:) Again, to that extent instant physical action in time is not the same kind of life-and-death factor that it was when a man was faced with an enraged animal, or enemy, in close combat. (“Can I ask a question?” As Seth, Jane nodded. “Will you give us a definition of what you mean by early man? I think readers would be interested.” I’d been hoping Seth would go into this. Still in trance, Jane nodded again when I had finished — and I had the distinct impression that I shouldn’t have interrupted her delivery.)", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第686节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "686", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1159", "zh": "就像意识产生物质层面一样，身为意识一部分的你，会继续并重新创造它。你的能量，就是来自第一次的创造，在那次创造中，意识集中了，而之前并没有。然后，你透过自己的创造也认识了自己、发展了自己，自动创造和维护你的物质环境，就像呼吸一样自然。你的身体形象和物质环境都是你内在自我延伸的具体化。", "en": "Now in the same way that consciousness originated the physical dimension, you as portions of consciousness continue to maintain and create it anew. Your source of energy is that first creation, in which consciousness focused, where before it had not. You also then know and develop yourselves through your own creations, and you automatically create and maintain your physical environment in the same manner that you breathe. Your physical image and your physical environment are both materialized extensions of your inner selves.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第338节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "338", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1172", "zh": "这个自己在继续存在，即使是组成肉体的原料也继续行动。行动把本身分化成各种自我（selves），接着探索经验的各个片刻点，因为每个新的自己实际上都是一个新的行动，一种原始的行动。", "en": "The self goes on. Even the stuff of the physical body however continues to act. Action divides itself into various selves, and then explores the moment points of experience, for each new self is indeed a new action, an original act.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第343节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "343", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B04", "title": "当自我把「自己」误当成全部", "note": "自我最容易犯的错，是把自己当成全部、把其他部分砍了头。当自我把目标和才能单独据为己有时，等于切断了与内我的连系，人也容易被「只有这辈子、生到死就绝灭」的狭隘观念关在自己接受的实相小圈子里。它会因为一次退稿受伤就向外寻求补偿，会为了多要证明反而关上通灵的门、竖起只属于自我的屏障，也会在课前偶尔起来反抗、试图利用课程。把失败怪给命运或上帝、把罪过投射到一个「老天爷」形象上，也是同一种把责任推出去的旧做法。自我若坚持某种永久不变的稳定身份，注定失败——因为它本就是由行动组成的。", "src": "第 74、145、211、231、320、388、407、512、614、628、831 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 74 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 145 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 211 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 231 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 320 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 388 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 407 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 512 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 614 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 628 节"}, {"n": 11, "id": null, "label": "第 831 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-006-e0268", "zh": "当他的自我因一次退稿的事件而感到受伤时，他便向外寻求补偿。能量的狂潮，积极又充满了侵略性，突然在他工作的地方宣泄而出，哀鸿遍野。", "en": "He looks for satisfaction for his ego in the outside world when it has been bruised because of a rejection slip. Torrents of energy, both constructive and aggressive, suddenly are let loose where he works, and woe to all around.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第74节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "74", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e0468", "zh": "我即将说的东西有一部分听起来可能冷酷无情，但你应该明白实情并非如此。从忧心忡忡又煞费苦心的自我自己（ego-self）所在的观点，看起来真的是有巨大的、灾难性的罪恶，像毒药般满到溢出人类的生存之杯。 当他啜饮几口的时候，就像你已经啜饮过它那样，也像所有本着良心的人类啜饮它一样，其实味道是苦的。不过，再补充以下的话，也不算牵强：所有或很多药物不幸都有一种恶心的味道，啜饮这样一种药物的小孩会觉得难以相信，这么难喝的药水怎么可能对他有益处。", "en": "When he sips of it, as you have sipped of it, and as all conscientious human beings sip of it, then indeed the taste is bitter. It is not too farfetched however to add that all, or many, medicines have unfortunately a foul taste, and that the child who sips such a medicine finds it difficult to believe that such a distasteful brew can do him good. Basically, all action Basically there is no evil action. All is unfolding. With the limited perceptions that the ego has itself adopted, the whole is not visible, and it sees what it will see. Within your field, within your moral field, you must indeed strike out against that which appears evil to you.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第145节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "145", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e0817", "zh": "没有人会比我们的朋友鲁柏更想要证明，但常常当他有意识地想要更多证明的时候，就会关上了我来的门，设下了属于自我本身的屏障。", "en": "No one, you see, wants more proofs than our friend Ruburt, but often consciously he wants so much that he closes the doors through which I can come, and sets down barriers that belong to the ego alone.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第211节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "211", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e0876", "zh": "可以这么说，自我借由往回看进它过去的经验来保持它大部分的稳定性，在那里找到一些它自己。过去可能是一个幻相，但对自我来说，它并不是幻相。自己和可能性打交道的那部分并没有这样的经验，一个会让他们感觉到身份和连续性的过去的经验。", "en": "The ego maintains much of its stability by looking backwards, so to speak, into its experience of its past, and finding something of itself there. Now the past may be an illusion, but it is not illusion to the ego. The portions of the self that deal in probabilities do not have such an experience with a past, to give them their feeling of identity or continuity.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第231节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "231", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1139", "zh": "在我们的课当中，偶尔自我会起来反抗，但不到令人忧心的程度。在少数提到症状以及特定时间的情况下，这是自我在利用这些课的一个相当可悲的尝试。", "en": "Now occasionally the ego has risen up in our sessions, but to no alarming degree. On the few occasions when the symptoms were mentioned and a particular time given, this was a rather pathetic attempt on the part of the ego to make use of the sessions.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第320节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "320", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1198", "zh": "自由选择一直存在，目的始终是理解与发展，而不是惩罚，不是自我惩罚。这个女子过去的那一世，曾是意大利一个小山村的男子（停顿），后面我们会尝试补充时间、日期和地点的讯息。", "en": "Free choice is always involved. The purpose is always knowledge and development, rather than punishment, self punishment. The woman, in a past life, was once a man (pause), Italian, in a hill village. We will try to fill you in on times and dates and locations later.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第388节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "388", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1212", "zh": "他一直在阅读各部分资料，包括与自我、人格和行动等有关的部分，而且你看，他也试图将自身置于他整体人格紧密关联的行动之外。这就像自我平常试图坚持某种永久、不变、稳定的本体一样，不可能做得到，因为它是由行动所组成。", "en": "He has been reading various sections of the material, including portions having to do with the ego, personality and action, and you see attempted to set himself aside from the action in which his whole personality was intimately involved. As impossible [to do] as the ego’s general attempt to insist upon some sort of permanent, unchanging, stable identity, since it is composed of action.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第407节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "407", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1369", "zh": "如果你对实相的本质有一个狭隘的观念，那么你的自我会尽其所能地把你关在你所接受的实相的闭锁的小范围内。反过来说，如果你直觉的创造的本能被给予自由，那么它们会把对更广大次元的知识沟通给你人格的最朝向肉体的这一部分。", "en": "If you have a limited conception of the nature of reality, then your ego will do its best to keep you in the small enclosed area of your accepted reality. If, on the other hand, your intuitions and creative instincts are allowed freedom, then they communicate some knowledge of greater dimensions to this most physically oriented portion of your personality.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第512节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "512", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1556", "zh": "5.前生的际遇主宰了一切，我无能为力，因为今生我对前世发生的事情一点办法都没有。我必须受报应，或自我惩罚以求赎罪，谁叫我前世作孽。自作终归自受，自己造了“业”（karma）②，只好逆来顺受。", "en": "5. I am helpless because I am at the mercy of events from past lives in other incarnations, over which I now have no control. I must be punished, or I am punishing myself for unkindnesses done to others in past lives. I must accept the negative aspects of my life because of my karma.*", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第614节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "614", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1585", "zh": "奥古斯都曾被教以去害怕他自己的思想，去逃避自我反省，因此，那些使他惊吓的信念或者意念没能被面对，就被推到意识心的角落里去了。然而，在一开始，它们是相当无害地待在那里的。", "en": "Augustus had been taught to fear his own thoughts, to avoid self-examination. Beliefs or ideas that frightened him were not faced, therefore, but initially shoved into corners of the conscious mind, where they lay relatively harmlessly in the beginning.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第628节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "628", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1748", "zh": "既然一个人的特性、潜能及缺陷大半被看作是他无法掌握的机率、遗传及无意识机制的结果，那么他既不能为个人成就感到骄傲，也不能因为失败而被责难。比喻性的说，魔鬼走入了地下，因此魔鬼许多恶作剧的特质及邪恶的特性都被派给了无意识。人被视为自我分裂且与自己作对的东西——一个有意识的傀儡，很不安稳的歇在无意识的兽性上。他相信他自己是被遗传及早期环境定好了程式，以至于好像他永远必然对自己的真实动机无所知觉。", "en": "A person could neither be proud of personal achievement nor blamed for failure, since in large measure his characteristics, potentials, and lacks were seen as the result of chance, heredity, and of unconscious mechanisms over which he seemingly had little control. The devil went underground, figuratively speaking, so that many of his mischievous qualities and devious characteristics were assigned to the unconscious. Man was seen as divided against himself — a conscious figurehead, resting uneasily above the mighty haunches of unconscious beastliness. He believed himself to be programmed by his heredity and early environment, so that it seemed he must be forever unaware of his own true motives.4", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第831节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "831", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B05", "title": "自我与潜意识、内在感官：审查与屏障", "note": "自我和潜意识、内在感官之间始终是紧张的。内在感官不习惯如此自如地运作，常常让那个一直在场的自我感到烦恼甚至分心；外我天生与伪装模式打交道，所以面对一整套内在感官带来的了悟，它几乎承受不住那种震撼，于是严格审查、把很多讯息挡掉——梦境在它看来混乱或无意义，往往正是因为它删去了潜意识保留的内容。但这并不等于要消灭自我：你不能完全取代它，只能学着偶尔不聚焦在它上面，哄骗它，让内在感官透过自我的眼睛向外看；在睡眠与梦的状态里，你确实能觉察到那些被自我忽略的感知，有时两个自我还会在梦里彼此融合。", "src": "第 6、24、35、37、44、104、149、186、219、261、822 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 6 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 24 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 35 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 37 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 44 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 104 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 149 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 186 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 219 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 261 节"}, {"n": 11, "id": null, "label": "第 822 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-006-e0001", "zh": "片段体存有（Fragment entity），对现在的人格感到不自在。在自我和潜意识之间有缺口，生命力散失。他是他前世母亲存有的一部分。", "en": "Fragment entity, uneasy with present personality. Gap between （t no） ego and subconscious, vital forces escape. He is a part of his last mother’s entity.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第6节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "6", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e0049", "zh": "我以前就给你们解释过这件事。她在课前总是有点犹豫和怀疑，就像她自己曾经解释过，因为我是透过她来说话。内在感官不习惯如此自如地运作，而且这会让一直在场的自我感到烦恼，有时候似乎会使它分心。", "en": "（Jane dictates:） I explained this matter to you before. She is always slightly dubious and somewhat doubtful before a session, as she has explained herself, since she is the one through whom I speak. The inner senses are not accustomed to operating so freely and this upsets that all-present ego, and would seem sometimes to drive it to distraction.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第24节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "24", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e0121", "zh": "只有建立某种程度的信心，外在自我才有余力熟悉这些内在运作，至少在你们的层面是如此。否则，你们就会犹豫不前。原则上来说，即使全我有能力组织所有来自内在感官的资料，潜意识也很少能完完全全接收这样的讯息；而外在自我关注的是伪装模式，而且也的确是天生与伪装模式打交道，所以对整组内在感官带来的了悟，震撼得简直没办法法承受。", "en": "Only when a certain level of confidence is reached can the outer ego afford to become familiar with these inner workings, at least on your plane. Otherwise you would falter. As a rule, even though the whole self is capable of organizing the data from all of the inner senses, the subconscious can rarely receive such communications full blast; and the outer ego, concerned as it is with camouflage pattern, and really born to deal with camouflage pattern, simply could not stand the shock of realization that a complete set of inner senses would bring.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第35节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "35", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e0169", "zh": "个人永远会受到灾难的警告，这样有机体就能提前做好准备。死亡的日期是知晓的。意识上，基于明显可见的理由，这样的知识，不会给自我，但每个有机体，通过它的内在感官，具备个人灾难、死亡等潜意识知识，人格本身会事先决定它所认为的灾难；人类的成员整体而言都事先知道他们的战争。心灵感应持续在潜意识层运行，作为所有语言和沟通的基础，同样的，千里眼也在持续不断地运作，以使物质有机体可以做好准备去面对挑战。", "en": "Individuals are always warned of disasters, so that the organism can prepare itself ahead of time. The day of death is known. Consciously such knowledge is not given to the ego for obvious reasons, but every organism, through its inner senses, is equipped with subconscious knowledge of personal disasters, deaths, and so forth, the personality itself deciding beforehand what it considers disastrous; and the members of the species as a whole know in advance of their wars. As telepathy operates constantly at a subconscious level, as a basis for all language and communication, so clairvoyance operates continually so that the physical organism can prepare itself to face its challenges.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第44节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "44", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e0145", "zh": "你们不能完全取代它，除非你们把自己置于危险之中。不过你可以学着哄骗它。学会偶尔不要聚焦在它上面，而让内在感官通过自我的眼睛向外看。", "en": "You cannot displace it completely, except at your own peril. Nevertheless you can learn to trick it. You can learn to cease focusing now and then and let the inner senses look out through the ego's eyes.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第37节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "37", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e0346", "zh": "安静但坚定地，没有进一步与自我对抗，鲁伯借由暗示安全与慢动作，使它安静下来；和你怀疑的一样，慢动作暗示和（或）伴随预警，被潜意识相当巧妙地，也就是狡猾地解读，然后等待几个小时的适当间隔之后，才又再试了一次。", "en": "Quietly but firmly, without antagonizing the ego further, Ruburt quiet edit down by the suggestion of safety and slow motion; as you suspected the slow motion suggestion and/or coupled with the cautionary warning, was interpreted rather expertly, that is slyly, by the subconscious, which then waited a good interval of several hours before trying again.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第104节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "104", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e0499", "zh": "在很多方面，梦宇宙之内的行动，确实都比在你们自己的宇宙里更为直接。梦看起来有时候混乱或无意义，那是由于你们只记得浮光掠影的画面和支离破碎的情节，对自我来讲更是如此，因为自我严格审查很多潜意识保留下来的讯息。", "en": "In many respects actions within the dream universe are indeed more direct than in your own. It is because you remember but vague glimmerings and disconnected episodes that dreams appear, sometimes, chaotic or meaningless, particularly to the ego, which censors rigidly much of the information that the subconscious does retain.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第149节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "149", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e0739", "zh": "意识心、自我，一定要短暂退离，好让直觉的自己获得自由。他应该知道，灵感不是来自于自我。他的头脑对这一点很清楚，但在这种状况下，他坚持要把自我当成皮鞭，用来鞭策自己加快脚步。过去他比较能知觉到这一方面。", "en": "The conscious mind, the ego, must be momentarily diverted, so that the intuitive self is allowed freedom. He should know that inspiration does not come from the ego. He knows this intellectually, but upon this occasion he insists in using his ego as a whip to force speed. In the past he was more sensible in this respect.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第186节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "186", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e0837", "zh": "在梦的状态或意识的其他状态，他确实某种程度能觉察到只被自我所忽略的感知。换句话说，心理上自己A只有一部分对物质维度的感知是局限的，而那是自我。", "en": "In the dreaming state and in other states of consciousness, he can indeed to some degree become aware of perceptions which will be neglected by the ego alone. In other words, psychologically there is only one portion of self A that is limited in its perceptions to the physical dimension, and that is the ego.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第219节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "219", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e0977", "zh": "有效投射的质量确实是来自梦体。当游历结束时，回到梦体是不费力的，你看，因为自我几乎不参与。无论如何，在大多数这类情况下。这个知识对醒时的自己来说根本是不可得的。", "en": "The mass of valid projections are indeed made from the dreaming body. When the excursion is over the return to the dream body is made with no strain, you see, for the ego is little concerned. In most such instances however the knowledge is then not available to the waking self at all.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第261节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "261", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1733", "zh": "以那种说法，这未区分的地带实际上是充满了活动的，在那儿做出了心理上的转移与转译，直到在梦里这两个自我常常彼此融合起来——因而，你有时会带着一种短暂的兴高采烈的感觉醒来，或是带着在梦中你遇到了一个你重视的老朋友的感觉醒来。", "en": "In those terms the undifferentiated area is actually filled with motion as psychological transitions and translations are made, until in dreams the two egos often merge into each other — so that sometimes you waken briefly with a sense of elation, or a feeling that in dreams you have met an old and valued friend.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第822节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "822", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B06", "title": "一个健康、平衡的自我长什么样", "note": "一个健康、平衡的自我不是被消灭的自我，而是通情达理、甚至有纪律的那一个：它清楚自己的位置，也知道自己对整体的依赖，明白自己那种独特的孤立其实是整体完形的一部分。理智认识自我，是内我与自我之间一条稳固可靠的桥；自我也会学习和扩展，去接纳并运用新讯息，把暗示、投射这类活动用在它所认可、自觉负责的心理结构上。无论是透过迷幻经验整理新旧资料，还是像所有生物天生就有的那种深刻的自我认可感，重点都是让外我在放松中感到被支撑——它终究是「一切万有」高度专门化、让你得以解读特定状况的那一片。", "src": "第 90、160、234、306、457、469、681 节，及《健康之道》第 2、3 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 90 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 160 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 234 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 306 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 457 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 469 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 681 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 2 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 3 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-006-e0315", "zh": "这个人格也含有很好的智力能力，他也应该从智识的角度检视心灵经验。是有理智无法感知的真相，但理智认识自我，也代表着内我和自我之间一条稳固可靠的途径；而心灵经验——我再说一次，心灵经验不会因为这样的仔细调查而受苦。", "en": "The personality also contains good intellectual capacities, and he should examine psychic experience in the light of his intelligence also. There are truths which the intellect cannot perceive, but the intellect knows the ego, and represents a firm and reliable pathway between the inner self and the ego; and psychic experience—I repeat, psychic experience—will not suffer from such scrutiny.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第90节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "90", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e0579", "zh": "因为暗示持续不断地用在你们体内的每个细胞，所以问题不在于你们能不能使用暗示，而是如何更有效率地使用。这会牵涉到一个平衡的人格，因为在这样的人格当中，行动会获得表达的自由，自我在这过程中会有所得，而不是有所失，但我们的自我不会独裁专制，而是通情达理，甚至有纪律，不但明白自身的处境，还知道自身的依靠，也能深知到自身特有的孤立现象，因为这种孤立取决于它是整体完形的一部分。", "en": "Since suggestion is used constantly, and by every cell in your body, then it is not a question of whether or not you can use suggestion, but of how to use it more effectively. And this will involve a balanced personality, for in such a personality action will be allowed freedom of expression. The ego will gain and not lose in the process, but we will not have an autocratic and willful ego, but a reasonable and even disciplined ego that is aware of its position, aware of its own dependency, as well as of its own peculiar and unique perceptive apartness. For the apartness is dependent upon its being a part of the whole gestalt.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第160节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "160", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e0895", "zh": "再一次，可能性的领域并不是由富有想像力的想像或模糊的活动所组成的。它和物质宇宙是同样的真实。由自己其他部分所遭遇的经验会被全我所使用，而从中获得的知识是极其宝贵的。不只是就整体的经验来说，也是作为自我和潜意识从不同的活动之间选择一种训练方法。", "en": "Once more, the field of probabilities does not consist of imaginative fancy, nor of nebulous activity. It is quite as real as the physical universe. The experiences that are encountered there by other portions of the self are used by the whole self, and the knowledge thus gains is invaluable. Not only in terms of overall experience, but also as a means of training the ego, and the subconscious, to choose between various activities.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第234节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "234", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1081", "zh": "在这些情况下的迷幻经验也以有益的方式转化自我。不然的话，自我就被抛在后头，无法执行——现在作为一个规则——它的主要功能。当自我作为全我的一部分经历一个迷幻体验时，它能够组织旧的资料。然后它也可以组织新的资料。", "en": "The psychedelic experience under these circumstances transforms the ego also in beneficial ways. Otherwise the ego is left behind, unable to perform, as a rule now, its primary functions. The ego can organize the old data when it undergoes a psychedelic experience as a part of the whole self. Then it can also organize the new data.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第306节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "306", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1282", "zh": "他完全有自由质疑这些课的根基，质疑我本身的源头。（停顿。）可当他不信自己的时候，当他不信这资料中直觉的、启示性的面向的时候，他连质疑都不曾带着真正的逻辑。如今他的理智正在接受这资料的启示性面向，而他自己的相关文字里头一次出现了这个词（最近）。这词于他极富唤起力；而甚至他的理智也一向信任启示性的知识——只要这知识是经由自我所能接受的渠道交付给他的。（语气加重。）", "en": "He is quite free to question the basis of the sessions, and to question my own source. (Pause.) But he did not even do this with any true (underlined) logic, while he distrusted himself, or distrusted the intuitive and revelationary (underlined) aspect of the material. Now his intellect is accepting the revelationary aspect of the material, and the word appeared in his own writings about it for the first time. (Recently.) It is a highly evocative word to him, and even his intellect has always trusted revelationary knowledge as long as it was given to him through channels that were egotistically accepted. (Emphatic delivery.)", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第457节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "457", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1312", "zh": "系统中始终备有的蛰伏潜能，会随需要而被激活。诚然，物质的自己有时会有些不知所措，但自我也在学习、在扩展，从而能够接受并运用新的讯息、从中获益。例如它会迅速地学会种种方法，把这类活动用于它所认可、并自觉负有责任的那些心理结构的目的。", "en": "Latent potentialities, always present within the system, are activated as they are needed. The physical self can, it is true, become somewhat bewildered, but the ego also learns and expands so that it is able to accept and use the new information, and benefit from it. It quickly learns methods for example to utilize such activities for the purposes of the psychological structures that it recognizes and feels responsible for.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第469节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "469", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1648", "zh": "（“可是，这些选择是建立在你们对过去与现在之改变中的看法上。因为我比你们有一个更大的知觉范围，我就比较能预言将发生什么。但这是依赖我对你们将做的选择之预言，而选择仍然是你们自己的……选择之本身并没有与自由意志的理论相冲突，虽然自由意志所依赖的要比任何一个单独自我的自由要多得多了。如果自我被容许做所有的抉择，而自己的其他层面没有任何否决权的话，你们真的全都会在一种悲惨的处境了。", "en": "“I can, therefore, perceive far more than you can of your own future. I am hardly omnipotent, however. Nor, strictly speaking, is such omnipotence possible.” 7. As an artist, my intuitive reaction to Seth’s remark that an atom can move in more than one direction at once was to associate that ability with his notions of simultaneous time and probabilities. The artist, since he isn’t any kind of a scientist (even though he might be interested in science in general), attempts to grapple with the statement as best he can, in light of the feeling he has for what Seth is trying to say. At the same time he realizes that from his artistic viewpoint he may not be able to understand the paradox of “contradictory” motions.", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第681节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "681", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1792", "zh": "书的口授。（停顿良久，然后十分缓慢地：）那么，所有的生物也都天生具有一种深刻的自我认可感。", "en": "Book dictation. (Long pause, then quite slowly:) All creatures are also born, then, with a keen sense of self-approval.", "source": "健康之道 · 第2节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "2", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1800", "zh": "当然，事情并不需要如此。自我了解和自知可能可以改善个人的生活，不论他们生活的活动或情况。是真的，这些个人的确替自己选择了一个小心计划与规律化的生活风格，在其中，他个人地及经常地遭遇死亡的威胁；每天都变成一个漫长的探索过程，在其中他有意地衡量死亡和生命。就是如此。", "en": "This need not be the case, of course. Self-understanding and self-knowledge may be able to change the individuals’ lives for the better, regardless of their activities or conditions of life. It is true that these individuals do choose for themselves a carefully planned and regulated style of life, in which the threat of death is encountered personally and regularly; each day becomes an odyssey, in which death and life are purposefully weighed. Period.", "source": "健康之道 · 第3节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "3", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1807", "zh": "它也觉察组成它存在的布料本身之无限力量与力气。借由使得外在自我觉察到这些事实，它也能开始感觉一种加快的支持与滋润感。那知识能让它放松、放下，因此它感觉其生命被支撑与安全，而知道自己的确是宇宙之一个被挚爱的孩子，同时既古老又年轻，有着一个远超过时间历史的身份。", "en": "(Pause at 4:33.) It is also aware of the infinite power and strength that composes the very fabric of its being. Through being made aware of these facts, the exterior ego can begin to feel a quicker sense of support and nourishment. The knowledge can let it relax, let go, so that it feels its life couched and safe, and knows itself to be indeed a beloved child of the universe, both ancient and young at once, with an identity far beyond the annals of time.", "source": "健康之道 · 第3节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "3", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B07", "title": "自我与人类「神」观念的浮现", "note": "人类「神」的观念，是和意识的发展携手出现的。正在浮现的自我需要感觉自己的主控性与主宰性，于是想象出一个与自然分开、由它自己投射出去的主宰性神明——那个神带着它所有的光辉、野蛮、力量与统御企图，本质上是人正在浮现之自我的反映。十二门徒代表的十二种特质，正是连在「自我取向」上的主要特性，它们一面被吸向外在的日常实相，一面又环绕着内我运行。西方传统里被鼓励出来的「男性自我取向」特征，也让神祇变成好胜、男性化的。赛斯特意安抚：建立在自我中心的个人并没有什么不对，你的个体性不是该被丢掉的东西——他反对的是把「一个自我、一个身体、一个世界」当成唯一真相。", "src": "第 26、511、560、587、687、689、705、772 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 26 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 511 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 560 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 587 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 687 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 689 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 705 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 772 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-006-e0073", "zh": "另一方面，多细胞群组一开始在具有某种复杂程度的场域模式中形成时，人类意识就开始了。就人类意识而言，并没有一个明确的进入点，但有之前人类意识本身并不存在的一个点。自我意识的确存在。在山顶洞人（caveman）身上，你们所说的身为人的意识已经充分发展，但是——我再怎么强调这一点都不够——人类的生存概念来自于鱼类。", "en": "The beginnings of human consciousness, on the other hand, began as soon as multicellular groupings began to form in field patterns of a certain complexity. While there was no specific point of entry as far as human consciousness was concerned, there was a point before which human consciousness as such did not exist. Self-consciousness did exist. The consciousness of being human in your terms was fully developed in the caveman, but—and I cannot emphasize this enough—the human conception was alive in the fish.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第26节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "26", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1357", "zh": "这礼物附带了责任，但你们多半喜欢对你们生活中的成功自我庆贺，而将失败归罪于上帝、命运或社会。同样地，人类有一种倾向，把他自己的罪或过错投射在一个“老天爷”的形象上，看来老天爷他对这么多抱怨一定厌烦透了。", "en": "The gift brings a responsibility, and many of you are tempted to congratulate yourselves on the successes of your lives, and blame God, fate, and society for your failures. In like manner, mankind has a tendency to project his own guilt and his own errors upon a father-god image, who it seems must grow weary of so many complaints.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第511节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "511", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1405", "zh": "十二个门徒中的每一个都各自代表了属于一个人的不同特质，而你们所知的基督代表了“内我”。因此，十二门徒加上你们所知的基督（三位一体的那一位）代表了一个俗世人格——内我——以及与人的自我相连的十二个主要特性。就像基督为十二门徒所环绕，内我也是由这些物质取向的特性所环绕，每一属性一方面被吸引向外，倾注于日常的实相，却又环绕着内我而运行。", "en": "Each of the twelve represented qualities of personality that belong to one individual, and Christ as you know him represented the inner self. The twelve, therefore, plus Christ as you know him (the one figure composed of the three) represented an individual earthly personality — the inner self — and twelve main characteristics connected with the egotistical self. As Christ was surrounded by the disciples, so the inner self is surrounded by these physically oriented characteristics, each drawn outward toward daily reality on the one hand, and yet orbiting the inner self.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第560节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "560", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1429", "zh": "因此，“神”变成一个投射出去的概念，与个人无干，与“大自然”也分了家。它变成人的正在浮现的“自我”之反映，带着它所有的光辉、野蛮、力量与统御的企图。纵然有其明显的不利，这个探险却是极富创造性的，代表意识的一个“进化”，丰富了人的主观经验，而的确增益了实相的幅度本身。", "en": "God, therefore, became an idea projected outward, independent of the individual, divorced from nature. He became the reflection of man’s emerging ego, with all of its brilliance, savagery, power, and intent for mastery. The adventure was a highly creative one despite the obvious disadvantages, and represented an “evolution” of consciousness that enriched man’s subjective experience, and indeed added to the dimensions of reality itself.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第587节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "587", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1660", "zh": "你们所拥有对神的观念与你们意识的发展是携手并进的。正在浮现的自我需要感觉它自己的主控性与主宰性，因而，它想象出一个与自然分开的主宰性神明。国家常常像是集体自我——每个有它自己神的形象，它自己对力量的观念。每当一个部落、一个团体或一个国家决定要发动一次战争时，它永远用它的神明观念去领头。", "en": "There is nothing wrong with the concept of an egotistically based individual being, colon: I am not suggesting, therefore, that your individuality is something to be lost, thrown aside, or superseded. Nor am I saying that it should be buried, submerged, or dissolved in a superself. I am not suggesting that its edges be blurred by a powerful unconscious. (Intently:) I am saying that the individual self must become consciously aware of far more reality; that it must allow its recognition of identity to expand so that it includes previously unconscious knowledge. To do this you must understand, again, that man must move beyond the concepts of one god, one self, one body, one world, as these ideas are currently understood.5 You are now poised, in your terms, upon a threshold from which the race can go many ways. There are species of consciousness. Your species is in a time of change. There are potentials within the body’s mechanisms, in your terms, not as yet used. Developed, they can immeasurably enrich the race, and bring it to levels of spiritual and psychic and physical fulfillment. If some changes are not made, the race as such will not endure.", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第687节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "687", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1665", "zh": "对一个建立在自我中心的个人这观念并没什么不对；因此，我并没在建议你们的个人性是某些应该失去、抛在一边或被取代的东西。我也不是在说它应该被埋藏、淹没或溶入一个超我。我并没在建议它的边缘应被一个有力的无意识弄模糊。", "en": "And saved them, But the dreams were what I wanted.", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第687节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "687", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1671", "zh": "然而，那明确的专注产生了一个精美的焦点。而自我意识相较之下，则失去了部分的那种焦点。图腾柱始于那分离点之前，当人与动物仍彼此了解的时候。在那些时代存在并繁荣的具体物类于是对你们而言变成只是个可能性，因为它们没在你们的系统里发展，而绝种了。它们活生生的遗迹存在于那将它们具体表现出来的神明观念里。", "en": "The specific concentration, however, results in an exquisite focus. Ego consciousness lost part of that focus in comparison. The totem poles date back to the time when men and animals understood each other, before that point of departure. Physical species that existed and flourished in those epochs then became probable to you, for they did not develop in your system but became extinct. Their living relics exist in the god concepts that embodied them. Give us a moment …", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第689节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "689", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1683", "zh": "你们把一个高度演化的自我意识与你们自己族类的发展及你们自己那种感知的机制认同。不论何时，当你们检查任何其它种类的生命时，你们都把这些当作是法则或条件。在你们的可能系统里没有爬虫人，然而，在其它的可能性里，他们真的的确存在着，我提及这点，只不过是要告诉你们，你们所认知的演化系统只不过是这种系统之一而已。（热切的：）可是，其物质性的基础是潜伏在你们自己细胞结构之内的。你们认为演化已经结束，但是演化的动力是来自意识的本质本身之内的，它一直是如此。今天在某些地方很时兴说人的意识现在是一种新的演化里的一种因素——但那“新的意识”一直是潜在的，而你们只是现在才开始认识到它的存在。每一个意识都觉察它自己为它自己，那么，每个意识都是自我觉察的，它也许不是以跟你同样的方式自我觉察，它也许不会反思它自己的状况，然而，在另一方面来说，它也许没有那个需要。 请等我们一会儿……", "en": "You identify a highly evolved self-consciousness with your own species development, and with your own kind of perceptive mechanisms. You apply these as rules or conditions whenever you examine any other kind of life. In your system of probabilities there are no reptilian men or women, yet in other probabilities they do indeed exist. I mention this only to show you that the evolutionary system you recognize is but one such system. (Intently:) The physical basis rests latently within your own cellular structure, however. You think that evolution is finished. Its impetus, however, comes from within the nature of consciousness itself. It always has. In some quarters it is fashionable these days to say that man’s consciousness is now an element in a new kind of evolution — but that “new consciousness” has always been inherent. You are only now beginning to recognize its existence. Every consciousness is aware of itself as itself.5 Each consciousness, then, is self-aware. It may not be self-aware in the same way that you are. It may not reflect upon its own condition. On the other hand, it may have no need to.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第705节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "705", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1718", "zh": "你们所认为的男性自我取向的特征，只不过是族类所鼓励的那些人类属性，被带到前景来，而予以强制。实际上，你们长久以来用那些你们作为指导原则来看你们的世界，并形成你们的文化。也有些引人瞩目的例外，但此地我是谈历史上的西方世界，连同它的罗马和希腊传统。于是你们的神祇变成男性的、好胜的。你们看见人类对抗自然，以及对抗人。你们认为希腊悲剧很伟大，因为他们如此坚定地成为你们信念的回音。人被看作以直接方式与他自己的父亲敌对。家庭关系变成这种信念的一面镜子，而那些信念于是当然被当作是关于人类情况的一个事实声明。你们因而有了一个非常两极化的男—女观念。", "en": "What you think of as (underlined) male ego-oriented characteristics are simply those human attributes that the species encouraged, brought into the foreground, and stressed. Using those actually as guidelines, you have so far viewed your world and formed your cultures. There are some exceptions of note, but here I am speaking historically of the Western world with its Roman and Greek heritage. Your gods became masculine then; competitive. You saw the species pitted against nature, and man pitted against man. You consider the Greek tragedies great because they echo so firmly your own beliefs. Man is seen in opposition in the most immediate fashion with his own father. Family relationships become a mirror of those beliefs, which are then of course taken as statements of fact concerning the human condition. You thus have a very polarized male-female concept.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第772节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "772", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B08", "title": "临终与死后：自我的命运", "note": "自我在肉体死亡后会不会消失？赛斯的答案是否定的，但形态会变。内我送出一个新的外我去进行新的冒险时，前一个自我仍有近乎无限的发展途径；新的自我清楚自己是从前一个的死亡里诞生的，带着喜悦也带着对那毁灭的恐惧，必须像小孩的自我一样慢慢形成。死后人格若想和还在物质系统里的人沟通，得先把自我暂时交还较大的主权，否则很难打动仍自我取向的那一方。赛斯用来和你们相处、让你们安心「自己死后继续存在」的，正是他非常喜欢的、最贴近世俗存在的那部分自我。就连细胞这一层，身份也早已在物质与非物质实相之间来回旅行太多次，根本不怕自己的死亡。", "src": "第 300、362、423、638、744、752、867 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 300 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 362 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 423 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 638 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 744 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 752 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 867 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-006-e1062", "zh": "它们只是看起来不一样而已。在大多数情况下，自我觉察不到它离开一个物质有机体，在另一个里面成长。这是一次投射。我跟你说过，成长的年岁是幻相。价值完成是宇宙的法则，它在里面的系统之内看起来像是成长。", "en": "They simply appear to be different. As a rule the ego is not aware of its departure from one physical organism and its growth into another. This is a projection. The years of growth, as I have told you, are illusion. Value fulfillment is the law of the universe, and it appears as growth within your system.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第300节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "300", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1185", "zh": "然而，他可能有一个新的开始，将是各种倾向的重新组合，结果会形成一个新的自我，这个新的自我由旧的自我诞生而来。必须像小孩的自我一样，慢慢形成。你知道，他想省掉很多步骤，所以才会碰到麻烦。", "en": "There is a possible new beginning for him, however, and it will be a new reorganization of tendencies that results in the formation of a new ego, born out of the old. (Long pause.) It must be formed slowly, as the child's ego is. He wanted to cut out too many steps, you see, hence his difficulty.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第362节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "362", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1252", "zh": "要理解你们的时间，我们就得完全进入它，因为除了你们对它的主观经验之外，它没有任何意义。（停顿。）我们觉知到它对你们意味着什么，也觉知到你们把它视为本体的一部分，仿佛自我存在于一条实线上两点之间的某处。一点代表出生，另一点代表死亡。", "en": "To understand your time, we would have to enter into it completely, for it has no meaning but for your subjective experience of it. (Pause.) We are aware of what it means to you, and that you consider it a part of your identity, as if the self existed somewhere between two points, on a solid line. One point representing a birth, and another a death.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第423节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "423", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1599", "zh": "新的自我对它出生的情况相当了解，它知道自己是由前一个自我死亡中诞生的，虽然在它出生时，会感受到一股很大的喜悦，却对自己由之生出的那个毁灭感到恐惧。", "en": "The new ego is quite aware of the conditions of its birth. It knows it was born out of the death of its predecessor, and for all its feelings of transcendent joy, natural enough at its birth, it fears that annihilation from which it sprang.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第638节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "638", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1704", "zh": "当通讯发生在一个死后人格与一个存在于物质系统之内的人之间时，这涉及了死后人格那方面的一个重新排列，在那儿自我暂时被赋予较大的主权……如果这没被做到，那么，在大多数例子里，沟通将不可能，只因为那死后人格很难令仍是自我取向于物质系统之内的人格产生感应。", "en": "When communication takes place between a survival personality and one who exists within the physical system, this involves a reshuffling on the part of the survival personality, where the ego is momentarily given greater reign … If this was not done, then in most cases communication would not be possible, just because the survival personality would have such difficulty impressing the personality who was still ego-oriented within the physical system.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第744节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "744", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1708", "zh": "且说，我与你（及鲁柏）的关系的确是很奇怪的一个，因为你们与我的关系和你们彼此之间的关系并不相同。那些我显示的——我希望——令人愉快的人类自我性之特质有助于安抚你们的恐惧，并且让你们看到如你们所认为的“自己”（在肉体死亡之后）继续存在。我有一个很大的人格库藏可以汲取，而身为老师，我用在任何既定的实相系统里最有效的那个：而这是我在这儿用的一个。这是与世俗存在最密切相连的我自己那部分，而它真的是我非常喜欢的一个自己。", "en": "Now my relationship with you [and Ruburt] is indeed a strange one, since you do not relate to me as you do to each other. The — I hope — delightfully human egotistical characteristics that I show help calm your fears and show you that the self as you think of it continues to exist [after physical death]. I have a reservoir of personality banks upon which I can draw, and as a teacher I use the one that is most effective in any given system of reality; this is the one I use here. It is a portion of myself that is the most closely connected with earthly existence, and it is a self that I liked very well, indeed.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第744节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "744", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1713", "zh": "你的生命似乎与你的意识同义。因此看起来好像你对自己的知识是渐渐增长的，就如你的自我意识是从你出生而开始发展一样。更进一步，看来似乎你的意识将遭遇死亡，过了那一点你的自我意识就无法幸存。对你儿时的宗教，你可能怀着一种几乎是充满希望的怀恋，忆起一种保证你得永生的信仰体系。然而大部分的读者，却渴望着某些私密的和亲密的保证，并寻求某种内在的肯定，以确知自己的个人性（individuality）不至于在死亡时被粗鲁地开革（开除）（Yet most of you， my readers， yearn for some private and intimate assurances， and seek for some inner certainty that your own individuality is not curtly dismissed at（be dismissed at sometime：在某个时间被解雇，开除） death.）。", "en": "Your life seems synonymous with your consciousness. Therefore it appears that your knowledge of yourself grows gradually, as your self-consciousness develops from your birth. It appears, furthermore, that your consciousness will meet a death beyond which your self-consciousness will not survive. You may think longingly and with an almost hopeful nostalgia of the religion of your childhood, and remember a system of belief that ensured you of immortality. Yet most of you, my readers, yearn for some private and intimate assurances, and seek for some inner certainty that your own individuality is not curtly dismissed at death.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第752节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "752", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1753", "zh": "就像你们的想象力在生活中的每个领域都是那么重要，你们的想象力与疾病也是密切相连的。你借由想象性的考虑这样或那样的一个可能性而形成你的存在，而你的思想也以那种方式影响你的身体。以一种方式而言，疾病代表了生命的一种工具，因为人们已经给了疾病社会的、经济的、心理的及宗教的含义，因此它变成了另一个活动与表达的领域。 我告诉过你，在微观的层面并没有像你们自己的那种固定的自我结构。身分的确是有的。一个细胞并不害怕自己的死亡。它的身分已经理所当然的在物质实相和无形实相之间来回旅行太多次了。", "en": "I have told you that at microscopic levels there is no rigid (underlined) self-structure like your own. There is identity. A cell does not fear its own death. Its identity has traveled back and forth from physical to nonphysical reality too often as a matter of course.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第867节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "867", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B09", "title": "实操：怎么跟你的自我合作", "note": "和你的自我合作，靠的是「哄」而不是「灭」。你可以学着偶尔不把注意力聚焦在它上面，让内在感官透过它的眼睛向外看；自我暗示是最好用的钥匙——睡前那半小时左右的放松扩张阶段，暗示最有效，它能把你放进更直觉的心智模式。把信念当成自我催眠来用：你相信自己会生病，身体就真的病；反过来，想要健康的意图也能让细胞改变自我形象、强化自愈。跟随感受而不是压抑它们，会引出一连串的自我发现；解离（出神）并不比自我暗示更具束缚，你随时可以一瞬间把注意力拉回身体。这些都不是要你抛弃自我，而是让它学会放松、放下，感到被整个宇宙支撑。", "src": "第 199、205、289、644、660、707、744 节，及《健康之道》第 6 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 199 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 205 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 289 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 644 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 660 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 707 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 744 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 6 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-006-e0779", "zh": "第二个梦源自于自我暗示，它是疗愈梦的绝佳例子。鲁柏向他的内我要求了一个疗愈梦而他收到了。", "en": "The second dream is an excellent example of a therapeutic dream that results from self-suggestion. Ruburt requested a therapeutic dream from his inner self, and he received one.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第199节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "199", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e0798", "zh": "这很难诉诸语言。不要想到我们，要感觉我们，让我们看看可以怎么做。如果可能，自我暗示是最有利的，那会把你放在心智的一个较直觉的模式下。把你的情感转向我们，那我想我们就能接收到你的物件。", "en": "This is difficult to put into words. Feel toward us rather than think at us, and let us see how we do. Self-suggestion may be most beneficial when possible, when used to put you in this more intuitive frame of mind. Turn your emotions towards us, and I think we’ll be able to pick up your objects.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第205节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "205", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1043", "zh": "时间混乱（time scramble）总是有的，因为内在感官是在广阔的现在与基本资料打交道，一个中和的元素将会发展出来，保护鲁柏免于前几天晚上他所经历的那种情感电荷的全面冲击。有机体本身形成这个自我保护机制。", "en": "There is always a time scramble, for the inner senses deal with basic data in the spacious present . Then the data must be interpreted in the time scheme of physical existence. (Long pause.) With training and experience a neutralizing element will be developed that protects Ruburt against the full Emotional charge that he experienced the other evening. The organism itself forms this as a self protective mechanism.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第289节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "289", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1614", "zh": "借着认识这些区别，并诚实地从头到尾跟着你的感觉走——换句话说，借着顺应这些情绪——你会被领到在它们背后的信念中。这不可避免会导致一连串的自我发现，而其中每个都会把你导向更进一步的创造性心理活动。每一个阶段，你都会前所未有地更接近经验的实相，当意识心变得愈来愈觉知自己对事件发展的影响时，会得到很大的益处，它就不再害怕情感或身体，把它们当作具有威胁性或不可预料了，而感觉到自己卷入一个更大的统一里。", "en": "By recognizing these differences and honestly following the feelings through — in other words, by riding the emotions — you will be led to the beliefs behind them. A series of self-revelations will inevitably result, each leading you to further creative psychological activity. At each stage you will be closer to the reality of your experience than you have ever been.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第644节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "644", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1628", "zh": "他完全相信，如果他吃了禁食的食物之后就会生病，而事实上也是如此。但是他从来没有想到放弃那个信念——去了解正是这个信念本身，透过自我催眠的作用而建立了制约过程。", "en": "He fully believes he will become ill if he eats the forbidden foods, and so he does. It never occurs to him to dispense with the belief — to realize that it alone sets up the conditioning process through the operation of self-hypnotism.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第660节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "660", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1687", "zh": "你真的可以在健康与疾病之间作选择：在较集中于精神上而非物质上或较集中于物质上而非精神上作一个选择。这种私人的决定影响了人类的基因遗传。你的意图是最重要的——因为你可以在某个限度内改变你自己基因的讯息，举例来说，你可以使得一个细胞或一群细胞改变它们的自我形象：而另一方面，你常常在这样做——当你治愈了自己的疾病，因为你有一个想要变得健康的意图。那个意图会是有意识的，虽然那个方法不一定会是。不过，在这样一个例子里，细胞自愈的特性被加强了，而人类自愈的能力也被加强了。", "en": "You can literally choose between health and illness; between a concentration upon the mental more than the physical, or upon the physical more than the mental. Such private decisions affect the genetic heritage of the species. Your intent is all-important — for you can alter your own genetic messages3 within certain limits. You can cause a cell, or a group of cells, to change their self-image, for example; and again, you do this often — as you healed yourselves of diseases because of your intent to become well. The intent will be conscious, though the means may not be. Period. In such a case, however, the self-healing qualities of the cells are reinforced, and the self-healing abilities of the species are also strengthened.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第707节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "707", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1700", "zh": "我的确依赖鲁柏愿意离体（dissociate）的意愿。毫无疑问，有时候在一节课里他对周遭是不觉察的。不过，这并不比自我暗示对他有更大的束缚。这是一个他同意了的现象，而他能在任何时候，并且在一瞬间，令他有意识的注意力回到他的物质环境上。", "en": "I do depend upon Ruburt’s willingness to dissociate.12 There is no doubt that at times he is unaware of his surroundings during a session. However, this is no more binding upon him than autosuggestion. It is a phenomenon in which he gives consent, and he could, at any time and in a split second, return his conscious attention upon his physical environment.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第744节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "744", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-006-e1815", "zh": "今天下午，我也许会也许不会回来。但无论如何，我已启动那些如此鼓励自我疗愈、信心及幸福的坐标。", "en": "I may or may not return this afternoon, but in any case I have activated those coordinates that so encourage self-healing, faith, and well-being.", "source": "健康之道 · 第6节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "6", "only_en": false}]}]}], "reading": [], "books": [{"name": "早期课第1册", "count": 7}, {"name": "早期课第5册", "count": 7}, {"name": "早期课第6册", "count": 7}, {"name": "灵魂永生", "count": 6}, {"name": "早期课第2册", "count": 6}, {"name": "早期课第3册", "count": 6}, {"name": "早期课第8册", "count": 6}, {"name": "个人实相的本质", "count": 6}, {"name": "早期课第7册", "count": 5}, {"name": "早期课第9册", "count": 5}, {"name": "早期课第4册", "count": 5}, {"name": "个人与群体事件的本质", "count": 5}, {"name": "未知的实相卷一", "count": 5}, {"name": "未知的实相卷二", "count": 5}, {"name": "健康之道", "count": 4}, {"name": "时空之外", "count": 3}, {"name": "心灵的本质", "count": 2}, {"name": "梦、进化与价值完成", "count": 1}], "span": [1963, 1984], "stats": {"blocks": 9, "quotes": 91, "reading": 0, "reading_tagged": 0, "tagged": 0, "only_en": 2}};
